                <div style="color: #475569; margin-top: 3px;">Terminal Output: <code>&gt; Plain: 'secret123' ➔ SHA-256 Hash: 'a665a45920...' • Verified: True</code></div>
            </div>
            <p class="mission-subtitle">Follow the step-by-step instructions below in the editor:</p>
            <div id="taskChecklist"></div>
        </article>
        
        <!-- Core Concept & Analogy -->
        <article class="concept-card">
            <h3><span>💡</span> Core Concept &amp; Mental Model</h3>
            <div class="analogy-callout">
                <strong>Real-World Analogy:</strong> Cryptographic hashing is like blending a fruit smoothie 🥤: you can easily turn strawberries and bananas into a smoothie (hash), but you can never turn the smoothie back into fresh whole fruit.
            </div>
        </article>

        
        <article class="concept-card">
            <h3><span>🔒</span> SHA-256 One-Way Hash Flow</h3>
            <div class="tag-demo">
                <div class="tag-example">
                    <div class="tag-code">hashlib.sha256(pw.encode())</div>
                    <div class="tag-result">Transforms string into 256-bit cryptographic digest</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tag-example">
                    <div class="tag-code">.hexdigest()</div>
                    <div class="tag-result">Produces 64-character hexadecimal representation</div>
                </div>
